<%# chrome-top swap region (data-flow-chrome="top"): server-rendered so BOTH
    the page (show.html.erb) and the in-place JSON responses (the
    in-place responses) can swap it without a full reload. i18n keys are
    explicit (plan_flows.show.*) — a partial's lazy scope is its own name.
    This region shrunk to the amber drift prompt
    only. The groups that used to live here moved to the toggle row in
    show.html.erb as compact hover icons (same @scenario / @over_plan_lines
    / @discrepancy_lines locals, same t() calls):
      - the amber scenario banner -> the yellow "i" icon's popup (the
        exact banner text + the Back to live plan link, same exit path);
      - the over-plan RED lines + the RED Un-Allocated
        discrepancies (@discrepancy_lines, strict >$1.00 tolerance) -> the
        red caution icon's popup (the exact line text, one item per line,
        over-plan lines first as before).
    The prompt stays here: it is amber (a prompt, not a mismatch) and
    the Re-apply button must remain reachable inside the chrome.top swap. %>
<div data-flow-chrome="top">
  <%# the stale-config prompt — amber, NOT red (a stale
      config is a prompt, not a mismatch); the Re-apply link re-opens the
      fun_money dialog so the user re-saves (the save re-pins the input
      snapshot). %>
  <% stale = @graph[:allocations]&.find { |row| row[:kind] == "fun_money" && row[:inputs_stale] } %>
  <% if stale %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-amber-600" data-flow-chrome-stale>
      <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>
        <%= t("plan_flows.show.inputs_stale") %>
        —
        <button type="button"
                class="underline hover:opacity-75"
                data-fm-stale-reapply
                data-fm-stale-allocation="<%= stale[:id] %>">
          <%= t("plan_flows.show.inputs_stale_reapply") %>
        </button>
      </span>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
